    "rationale": "A limited paradigm network is defensible for the procedure codes with clear compositional structure. Two productive frames are supported: (i) no-face procedure + duration, seen in rot12/ws12/cc12/fan12/board12/rest12/cover12 and WBt#; and (ii) face-indexed procedure + face + duration, seen in C[f]t#, W[f]t#, CV[f]t#, R[f]t#, L[f]t#, BD[f]t#, RS[f]t#, WC[f]t#, HC[f]t#, CE[f]t#, RW[f]t#, RT[f]t#, FA[f]t#, and S6[f]t#. In both, the procedure slot shows strong substitution contrasts in a shared frame, and the duration/face pieces contribute stable meanings. Other apparent repetitions (e.g. final g/m, x#, bracketed face-pairs, initial bigrams in symptom codes) were rejected because they lack a secure same-frame alternation with predictable whole meanings in this dataset. All remaining symbols are treated as lexical.",
